-- title:
--   Verified gathering of independently flagged source histogram values
-- statement:
--   Let $m>0$, let endpoints $x_i\in\mathbb Z$ satisfy $|x_i|\le U$ for $i<n$, let $b_i\in\{0,1\}$, and let $H:[m]\to\mathbb N$ satisfy $H(r)\le B$. Suppose memory $\mu$ stores these arrays in segments ending at or before output base $z$. Let $z+n\le f$, $f+\lfloor\log_2(U+1)\rfloor+2\le S\le W$, $4U+4m+16\le W$, $B\le W$, and $d<D$. If $P$ contains the source-gather body and Euclidean-remainder helper, execution finishes within $n(R_U+80)+6$ steps, with $R_U=43(\lfloor\log_2(U+1)\rfloor+1)+34$, and stores
--
--   $$
--   \nu(z+i)=b_i H(x_i\bmod m)\quad(i<n).
--   $$
--
--   All addresses below $f$ outside $[z,z+n)$ are preserved. This gathers retained source weights from a precomputed histogram without recounting its original inputs.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightSourceGather.lean#L48-L133

